  "description": "Contract `12.7.0`'s asynchronous call and its fifth event kind, authored with no new tool and no new addressing: a require port on a client/server interface, a `calls` entry at its `(port, operation)` member address stating `asynchronous: true`, and a `call_returned` event at its own `whole_value` member address under a runnable's `events`, `{member: {type: call_returned, port, operation}}`, naming the same pair. The event is the call's result point, so the change set is accepted at AUTOSAR 4.2.2, where an asynchronous call point needs exactly one; a stated `result` or `name` joins the event's identity only when set.",
